  "description": "CUZXAZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C295 H389 Co6 Eu6 N6 O45 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.972-3.618 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.83-109.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C295H389Co6Eu6N6O45−·C6H16N+·2H2O.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
